ll,"entryId":null}]},{"ref":"90:19","translation":"But those who disbelieved in Our Ayât (proofs, evidence, verses, lessons, signs, revelations, etc.), they are those on the Left Hand (the dwellers of Hell).","translationSource":"qul-301-hilali-khan","notes":[],"tokens":[{"key":"90:19:1","position":1,"arabic":"وَٱلَّذِينَ","kind":"word","gloss":"But those who","transliteration":"wa-alladhīna","lemma":"الَّذِى","root":null,"entryId":"l-5016cb590bd9088a"},{"key":"90:19:2","position":2,"arabic":"كَفَرُوا۟","kind":"word","gloss":"disbelieve","transliteration":"kafarū","lemma":"كَفَرَ","root":"كفر","entryId":"l-f6f8e55e4806177f"},{"key":"90:19:3","position":3,"arabic":"بِـَٔايَـٰتِنَا","kind":"word","gloss":"in Our Verses","transliteration":"biāyātinā","lemma":"ءَايَة","root":"ايي","entryId":"l-5ab33552830ad5b5"},{"key":"90:19:4","position":4,"arabic":"هُمْ","kind":"word","gloss":"they","transliteration":"hum","lemma":null,"root":null,"entryId":null},{"key":"90:19:5","position":5,"arabic":"أَصْحَـٰبُ","kind":"word","gloss":"(are the) companions","transliteration":"aṣḥābu","lemma":"أَصْحَٰب","root":"صحب","entryId":"l-ab241d9510e7e8aa"},{"key":"90:19:6","position":6,"arabic":"ٱلْمَشْـَٔمَةِ","kind":"word","gloss":"(of) the left (hand)","transliteration":"l-mashamati","lemma":"مَشْـَٔمَة","root":"شام","entryId":null},{"key":"90:19:7","position":7,"arabic":"١٩","kind":"end-marker","gloss":"","transliteration":"","lemma":null,"root":null,"entryId":null}]},{"ref":"90:20","translation":"The Fire will be shut over them (i.e. they will be enveloped by the Fire without any opening or window or outlet.","translationSource":"qul-301-hilali-khan","notes":[{"text":"\"Therein breathing out with deep sighs and roaring will be their portion, and therein they will hear not. **\" [The Qur’ân, Verse 21:100] **Ibn Mas‘ûd رضي الله عنه recited this Verse and then said: \"When those (who are destined to remain in the Hell-fire forever) will be thrown in the Hell-fire, each of them will be put in a separate Tabût (Box) of Fire, so that he will not see anyone punished in the Hell-fire except he himself.\" Then Ibn Mas‘ûd recited this Verse (V.21:100). [Tafsîr Ibn Kathîr, Tabarî and Qurtubî].","ref":null}],"tokens":[{"key":"90:20:1","position":1,"arabic":"عَلَيْهِمْ","kind":"word","gloss":"Over them","transliteration":"ʿalayhim","lemma":"عَلَىٰ","root":null,"entryId":"l-08dd9283adb70e54"},{"key":"90:20:2","position":2,"arabic":"نَارٌۭ","kind":"word","gloss":"(will be the) Fire","transliteration":"nārun","lemma":"نَار","root":"نور","entryId":"l-1f4c1e0172701e6e"},{"key":"90:20:3","position":3,"arabic":"مُّؤْصَدَةٌۢ","kind":"word","gloss":"closed in","transliteration":"mu'ṣadatun","lemma":"مُّؤْصَدَة","root":"وصد","entryId":null},{"key":"90:20:4","position":4,"arabic":"٢٠","kind":"end-marker","gloss":"","transliteration":"","lemma":null,"root":null,"entryId":null}]}]